{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3.5-397b-a17b", "content": "**Chasing Cherry Blossoms in Kyoto**\n\nLast spring, I finally made the trip to Japan, and it exceeded every expectation. My journey began in Tokyo, a neon-lit labyrinth where ancient shrines sit quietly beside towering skyscrapers. The energy was electric, from the orderly chaos of Shibuya Crossing to the serene quiet of Meiji Shrine.\n\nHowever, the true magic happened when I boarded the Shinkansen to Kyoto. Riding the bullet train felt like stepping into the future, whisking me away to a city that time seems to have forgotten. The cherry blossoms were in full bloom, painting the Philosopher's Path in soft shades of pink. Walking under that floral canopy, with petals drifting down like snow, was a moment of pure tranquility.\n\nI spent my days exploring golden temples like Kinkaku-ji and wandering through the thousands of vermilion torii gates at Fushimi Inari. Each step revealed a new perspective, a hidden garden, or a friendly local offering a warm smile. The food was equally unforgettable; from steaming bowls of ramen in narrow alleys to delicate kaiseki dinners that looked too beautiful to eat.\n\nWhat struck me most was the blend of deep tradition and cutting-edge innovation. You can witness a centuries-old tea ceremony in the morning and visit a robot restaurant at night. Japan doesn't just offer a vacation; it offers a shift in perspective. As I boarded my flight home, I knew this wasn't a goodbye, but a \"see you later.\" The land of the rising sun has permanently captured a piece of my heart.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.029080803}, {"token": "Ch", "logprob": -0.029081479}, {"token": "asing", "logprob": -1.2360816}, {"token": " Cherry", "logprob": -4.279705e-05}, {"token": " Bloss", "logprob": -1.7881409e-06}, {"token": "oms", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.13153653}, {"token": " Kyoto", "logprob": -0.0019396866